      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "The local Gram determinant is |w(det A)|² det h_w≤D^N by Hadamard. Its product is |Norm(det A)|P(h). For k=h/c the primal minimum gives 1≤(4d)^d det G. The Gram determinant identity, d≥2, and |disc L|≥1 imply I₀P(k)≥1. Rescaling yields P(h)≥c^(Nr)/I₀. The determinant lemma in the source separately covers d=0.",
      "review": "An independent source reading confirmed the factors 2^d and |disc L|^N and the exponent Nr. The real dimension has no d=1 branch for a totally complex field."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCR-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Scaled inverse residues give a finite list under left multiplication",
      "anchor": "inputs-compact-residues",
      "statement": "For any number field L of degree e, integers N,J≥0, there is a list S of at most J^(1+eN²) integral N-by-N matrices. For each A with det A≠0 and |Norm(det A)|≤J, there exists g∈GL_N(𝒪_L) with gA∈S.",
      "hypotheses": "The argument uses the full ring of integers in an arbitrary number field and requires no assumption on its infinite places. At fixed determinant norm I the stratum has I≥1; J=0 gives the empty list.",
      "definitions": [
        "For |Norm(det A)|=I, the scaled inverse U=IA⁻¹ has integral entries since I∈(det A).",
        "The matrix U modulo I𝒪_L has at most I^(eN²) possible values.",
        "An orbit may occur for multiple residues; agreement of residues supplies an orbit witness."
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-compact-left-change"
      ],
