      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "Equal residues yield IA⁻¹−IA′⁻¹=IX. Then A′A⁻¹=Id+A′X and AA′⁻¹=Id−AX are inverse integral matrices. One lift per attained residue suffices. Sum the bounds for 1≤I≤J. The source may send an unattained key to zero and filters for nonzero determinant for the compact union.",
      "review": "Independently checked the order of left multiplication, the pointwise fixed-norm exponent and the exponent of the union. In the Gaussian worked example U−U′=2E₁₂ recovers g=Id+(1+i)E₁₂ and its inverse."
