    {
      "id": "FCR-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The finite matrix list indexes compact sets meeting all thick orbits",
      "anchor": "inputs-compact-pieces",
      "statement": "For every totally complex L, N≥1 and c>0 there exists a compact K inside the positive cone. Every positive h with λ(h),λ∨(h)≥c has a translate in K. The construction uses at most J^(1+[L:ℚ]N²) compact pieces for J=ceil(I₀(D/c)^(Nr)) and D=10C_T/c.",
      "hypotheses": "C_T=C_T(L,N) is the squared covering estimate constant. Both minima are squared and taken over the nonzero integral lattice. The list and K can be chosen independently of the form h.",
      "definitions": [
        "For nonsingular B on the finite list, impose lower constraints q_k(v)≥c for every integral v≠0 and upper constraints q_k(B_j)≤D for each column.",
        "A field basis of short columns need not be an integral basis.",
        "The finite family indexes sets of forms; each such set can hold a continuum of forms."
      ],
